<div class="sec"><h2>How League Pass blackouts work</h2></div>
<div class="dec">
<div class="dc"><span class="n">RULE 1</span><h3>Your home team</h3><p>If you live in a team's home market, its local games are blacked out on League Pass. They air on that team's local channel instead.</p></div>
<div class="dc"><span class="n">RULE 2</span><h3>National games</h3><p>Games on ESPN, ABC, NBC, Peacock and Prime Video are blacked out live on League Pass everywhere in the US.</p></div>
<div class="dc"><span class="n">RULE 3</span><h3>Everything else</h3><p>Out-of-market games that aren't national are on League Pass. That's most of the schedule for fans of a team in another city.</p></div>
</div>
<p class="fine">Some areas sit inside more than one team's market. Our ZIP map is a hand-built approximation; the <a href="{{ site.blackoutChecker }}" rel="nofollow noopener">NBA's blackout guide</a> is the final word.</p>
